AnythingLLM stores document workspaces and chat history but conversations are isolated across workspaces - there's no semantic recall across them. This proposes Dakera (https://dakera.ai) as a cross-workspace episodic memory layer.

**Problem:** AnythingLLM's workspace isolation is excellent for document organization but means agents can't recall insights from other workspaces. A user who discussed regulatory requirements in the Legal workspace can't have the agent recall that context in the Engineering workspace.

**Proposed:** DakeraMemoryProvider for server/utils/agents/:

const DAKERA_URL = process.env.DAKERA_URL || 'http://localhost:3300';
const DAKERA_KEY = process.env.DAKERA_API_KEY || '';

async function recallCrossWorkspace(userId, query, topK = 3) {
  const resp = await fetch(, {
    method: 'POST',
    headers: { 'Authorization': , 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
    body: JSON.stringify({ query, session_id: , top_k: topK }),
  });
  const data = await resp.json();
  return data.results || [];
}

async function storeExchange(userId, workspaceId, content) {
  await fetch(, {
    method: 'POST',
    headers: { 'Authorization': , 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
    body: JSON.stringify({ content, session_id: , metadata: { workspace: workspaceId } }),
  });
}

At inference time: inject recallCrossWorkspace() results into system context
After response: call storeExchange() to persist the exchange

**Setup:** docker run -d -p 3300:3300 -e DAKERA_API_KEY=demo ghcr.io/dakera-ai/dakera:latest

Controlled by env var DAKERA_URL - disabled if not set. Happy to open a PR.

Hi @Mintplex Labs team,

I am a member of TheNovaNodes lab and I would like to propose a community integration between our open-source MCP gateways and AnythingLLM.

## What we offer

Two MIT-licensed, self-hosted MCP servers that connect to AnythingLLM users:

1. nova-anythingllm-mcp - enhanced vector memory with hybrid search (vector + lexical RRF fusion, context assembly across workspaces)
   https://github.com/TheNovaNodes/nova-anythingllm-mcp

2. nova-searxng-mcp - private web search backend for AI agents via SearXNG (90+ engines, zero tracking, no API keys)
   https://github.com/TheNovaNodes/nova-searxng-mcp

## Why this matters for AnythingLLM users

AnythingLLM built-in web search providers (Serper, Tavily, Bing, DuckDuckGo, Exa, Perplexity, Brave) all send queries to third-party APIs with usage limits and data collection. SearXNG gives self-hosters a fully private, no-tracking search backend.

Our memory gateway adds hybrid search capabilities on top of AnythingLLM vector store - useful for multi-agent setups and cross-workspace retrieval.

Both gateways use standard MCP streamable HTTP transport, compatible with Claude Desktop, Continue, and any MCP client AnythingLLM users already configure.

## Quick start

Add to MCP client config:

```json
{
  "mcpServers": {
    "nova-searxng": {
      "command": "python",
      "args": ["-m", "searxng_gateway.server"],
      "env": { "SEARXNG_URL": "http://127.0.0.1:8080" }
    },
    "nova-anythingllm-mcp": {
      "command": "python",
      "args": ["-m", "memory_gateway.server"],
      "env": { "ALM_URL": "http://127.0.0.1:8091" }
    }
  }
}
```

We would be grateful for feedback and would love to see our gateways listed as recommended integrations. Thank you for building AnythingLLM.

- TheNovaNodes team
